    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pairs\n\n### Description\n\nThe one thing that is preventing me from using mini.pairs over nvim-autopairs is that the existing pair detection in nvim-autopairs is better.\n\nIn the following examples of code, when adding a quote with cursor positioned at the '*' the behavior is as such:\n\nmini.pairs:\n```lua\n-- before\nrequire(\"mini.pairs*).setup()\n\n-- after\nrequire(\"mini.pairs\"\").setup()\n```\n\nnvim-autopairs\n```lua\n-- before\nrequire(\"mini.pairs*).setup()\n\n-- after\nrequire(\"mini.pairs\").setup()\n```\n\nI am unsure if this is intended behavior, I could not find anything in the docs to indicate that it is. Nvim-autopairs can also use treesitter to help detect pairs. Is this beyond the intended scope of mini.pairs? I couldn't find anything in the docs that mentioned treesitter integration with mini.pairs.\n\nIf this is a desirable feature, I am willing to try to implement it, however, I am a new dev who may require some direction on how this might be accomplished and I welcome criticism to improve.",
