        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe current behavior is by design and [documented](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2431902e78b76f435542d1e606f08475360068ca/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L8-L9). Performing a more complex checks before deciding whether to insert a pair is not really performant compared to what there is now (only check based on the character to the left and right of the cursor). This is also [documented](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/2431902e78b76f435542d1e606f08475360068ca/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L21-L23).\n\n---\n\n> If this is a desirable feature, I am willing to try to implement it, however, I am a new dev who may require some direction on how this might be accomplished and I welcome criticism to improve.\n\nThat's an admirable spirit which I can only support. Sorry that this is not the feature that needs implementation.",
